---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="InTellMe"
  description="InTellMe is a research company in Johnson City, Tennessee. We build a checkpoint that AI systems run before they act, plus a few everyday apps that grew out of that work."
  path="/"
>

  <!-- ── HERO ───────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-line">
    <picture>
      <source media="(max-width: 1023px)" srcset="/assets/imagery/hero-material-1400.webp" />
      <img class="hero__still" src="/assets/imagery/hero-material.webp" alt=""
           width="2400" height="1350" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" />
    </picture>
    <div class="hero__veil" aria-hidden="true"></div>

    <div class="suite suite--flagship hero__inner">
      <h1 class="hero-line" id="hero-line">Before an AI acts on something, it should know whether it&rsquo;s true.</h1>
      <hr class="rule--champagne" />
      <p class="hero-support">InTellMe is a research company in Johnson City, Tennessee. We build a checkpoint that AI systems run before they take action. It looks at where their information came from and whether it holds up. We also make a few everyday apps that grew out of that work.</p>
      <div class="actions">
        <a class="btn btn--primary" href="https://truvector.science" rel="noopener">Visit TruVector</a>
        <a class="btn btn--secondary" href="/investors">For investors</a>
        <a class="btn btn--tertiary" href="https://www.researchone.io/" rel="noopener">Try ResearchOne <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">&#8594;</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── TECHNOLOGY ─────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="room" id="technology" aria-labelledby="technology-title">
    <div class="suite suite--flagship">
      <p class="kicker">What we build</p>
      <h2 class="suite-title reveal" id="technology-title">One problem, three pieces.</h2>

      <p class="lede reveal" style="margin-top:22px;max-width:66ch">AI systems are starting to act on their own: sending messages, approving requests, moving money, publishing content. They act on whatever information they pulled in, and a lot of that is wrong, out of date, or one rumor copied across dozens of sites. Lane Vector is the science of how information moves. TruVector is the product that uses it to check an AI&rsquo;s information before it acts. ResearchOne is a research workspace built on the same rules.</p>

      <div class="flagship" style="margin-top:48px">
        <div class="flagship__pane reveal">
          <div class="pane__head">
            <h3 class="product__mark--typeset" style="margin:0">Lane Vector</h3>
          </div>
          <p class="lede pane__lede">The science of how information moves.</p>
          <p style="margin-top:28px">Most tools count how often something shows up. Lane Vector measures which way it&rsquo;s moving, how fast, and whether many voices are really one voice repeated. One story copied five times is still one source, not five confirmations.</p>
          <div class="actions" style="margin-top:28px">
            <a class="btn btn--secondary" href="https://www.lanevector.com" rel="noopener">Open Lane Vector</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flagship__pane reveal">
          <div class="pane__head">
            <h3 class="product__mark--typeset" style="margin:0">TruVector</h3>
          </div>
          <p class="lede pane__lede">A checkpoint an AI system runs before it acts.</p>
          <ul class="states" aria-label="Possible answers">
            <li>Allow</li><li>Review</li><li>Block</li>
          </ul>
          <p style="margin-top:28px">Before the AI acts, TruVector checks three things: where the information came from, whether the sources are really separate or one source copied many times, and whether they agree. Then it answers Allow, Review (have a person look), or Block, with the reasons attached so someone can check them later.</p>
          <p>It works like a credit check, except it checks the information an AI is about to rely on instead of checking a borrower.</p>
          <p>It doesn&rsquo;t trust a source just because it&rsquo;s a big name. It looks at how the information actually got there.</p>
          <div class="actions" style="margin-top:28px">
            <a class="btn btn--secondary" href="https://truvector.science" rel="noopener">Open TruVector</a>
            <a class="btn btn--tertiary" href="/investors#request">Request the Technical Brief <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">&#8594;</span></a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flagship__pane reveal">
          <div class="pane__head">
            <svg class="product__mark" viewBox="0 0 240 240" role="img" aria-label="ResearchOne" style="height:34px;margin:0">
              <g transform="translate(120 120)" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-linecap="round">
                <polygon points="0,-110 95.3,-55 95.3,55 0,110 -95.3,55 -95.3,-55" stroke-width="7"></polygon>
                <path d="M -50,0 C -50,-40 50,-40 50,0 C 50,40 -50,40 -50,0" stroke-width="9"></path>
                <path d="M -40,12 C -40,-28 60,-28 60,12 C 60,52 -40,52 -40,12" stroke-width="9" opacity=".62"></path>
              </g>
            </svg>
            <h3 class="room-title" style="font-size:1.5rem">ResearchOne</h3>
          </div>
          <p class="lede pane__lede">A research workspace that keeps every source attached to what you write.</p>
          <ul class="facts">
            <li>Every claim links back to where it came from.</li>
            <li>When sources disagree, both sides stay in the report.</li>
            <li>You can see how each conclusion was reached.</li>
            <li>Reports follow a consistent, checkable format.</li>
          </ul>
          <div class="actions" style="margin-top:28px">
            <a class="btn btn--tertiary" href="https://www.researchone.io/" rel="noopener">Open ResearchOne <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">&#8594;</span></a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="technology-strip reveal" aria-label="Examples">
        <article class="illustration-card">
          <img class="illustration-card__img" src="/assets/imagery/examples/refund.svg" width="600" height="400" alt="An AI support chat about to issue a refund is checked against an old policy page and a current one that disagree, and the request goes to a person." loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          <p class="illustration-card__label">Example</p>
          <p class="illustration-card__body">An AI support agent is about to issue a refund based on a policy it found online. That page is three years old and the current policy says otherwise. TruVector sends it to a person instead.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="illustration-card">
          <img class="illustration-card__img" src="/assets/imagery/examples/reviews.svg" width="600" height="400" alt="A product page with a wall of five-star reviews; most of the reviews trace back to one cluster of sites, and only one comes from a separate customer." loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          <p class="illustration-card__label">Example</p>
          <p class="illustration-card__body">An AI shopping assistant finds 40 glowing reviews. Thirty-eight trace back to the same network of sites. TruVector flags it before the assistant recommends the product.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="illustration-card">
          <img class="illustration-card__img" src="/assets/imagery/examples/wire.svg" width="600" height="400" alt="One original news story at the center with many copies branching off it, counted as a single source." loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          <p class="illustration-card__label">Example</p>
          <p class="illustration-card__body">A news summary says &ldquo;reported by multiple outlets.&rdquo; They&rsquo;re all reprints of one wire story. TruVector counts it as one source.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── PRODUCTS ───────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="room room--alt" id="products" aria-labelledby="products-title">
    <div class="suite suite--flagship">
      <p class="kicker">Commercial ventures</p>
      <h2 class="suite-title reveal" id="products-title">Products that came out of the same work.</h2>

      <div class="rooms">
        <article class="product reveal">
          <img class="product__lockup" src="/assets/logos/savr.png"
               srcset="/assets/logos/savr.png 1x, /assets/logos/savr@2x.png 2x, /assets/logos/savr@3x.png 3x"
               width="163" height="72" alt="" />
          <div class="product__meta">
            <h3 class="visually-hidden">SAVR</h3>
          </div>
          <p class="product__body">AI-assisted kitchen inventory and recipe planning that turns what you already have into meals.</p>
          <div class="product__action">
            <a class="btn btn--tertiary" href="https://savr.cam" rel="noopener">Visit SAVR <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">&#8594;</span></a>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="product reveal">
          <img class="product__lockup" src="/assets/logos/golden-goose-tools.png"
               srcset="/assets/logos/golden-goose-tools.png 1x, /assets/logos/golden-goose-tools@2x.png 2x, /assets/logos/golden-goose-tools@3x.png 3x"
               width="107" height="72" alt="" />
          <div class="product__meta">
            <h3 class="visually-hidden">Golden Goose Tools</h3>
          </div>
          <p class="product__body">Instant technical SEO audit of a live page.</p>
          <div class="product__action">
            <a class="btn btn--tertiary" href="https://www.goldengoosetools.com/" rel="noopener">Run an SEO Audit <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">&#8594;</span></a>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="product reveal">
          <img class="product__lockup" src="/assets/logos/golden-goose-tees.png"
               srcset="/assets/logos/golden-goose-tees.png 1x, /assets/logos/golden-goose-tees@2x.png 2x, /assets/logos/golden-goose-tees@3x.png 3x"
               width="84" height="72" alt="" />
          <div class="product__meta">
            <h3 class="visually-hidden">Golden Goose Tees Studio</h3>
          </div>
          <p class="product__body">Design your own shirt with AI, see it on a mockup, and order it printed and shipped.</p>
          <div class="product__action">
            <a class="btn btn--tertiary" href="https://www.goldengoosetees.com/" rel="noopener">Open the storefront <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">&#8594;</span></a>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── RESEARCH ───────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="room" id="research" aria-labelledby="research-title">
    <div class="suite suite--flagship">
      <p class="kicker">Research</p>
      <h2 class="suite-title reveal" id="research-title">A public observatory for space and Earth data.</h2>

      <div class="research__grid reveal">
        <div>
          <div class="pane__head">
            <img class="product__lockup product__lockup--sm" src="/assets/logos/waether.png"
                 srcset="/assets/logos/waether.png 1x, /assets/logos/waether@2x.png 2x, /assets/logos/waether@3x.png 3x"
                 width="72" height="72" alt="" />
            <h3 class="visually-hidden">wAether</h3>
          </div>
          <p class="lede pane__lede">Solar, galactic, and terrestrial telemetry from official government sources, each named on the page where it appears.</p>
          <div class="actions" style="margin-top:28px">
            <a class="btn btn--secondary" href="https://www.waether.space" rel="noopener">Open wAether</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <ul class="sources" aria-label="Data sources">
            <li>NOAA SWPC</li><li>USGS</li><li>NASA DONKI</li><li>NOAA OVATION</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="caption" style="margin-top:24px">Pricing starts at $4.99/month or $49.99/year.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── COMPANY ────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="room room--alt" id="company" aria-labelledby="company-title">
    <div class="suite suite--flagship">
      <p class="kicker">Company</p>
      <h2 class="suite-title reveal" id="company-title">Built and run by Michael Brandon Lane.</h2>

      <div class="founder reveal">
        <p class="lede">InTellMe is an independent research and software company founded and operated by Michael Brandon Lane, a chemical engineer and chemist based in Johnson City, Tennessee.</p>

        <p>Before InTellMe, Lane worked at Celgard on lithium-ion battery separator and coating technology, including the development and scale-up of coated separator systems for high-volume manufacturing. He is a named inventor on multiple Celgard patents covering coated battery separators, including <a href="https://patents.google.com/patent/US11949124B2/en" rel="noopener">U.S. Patent 11,949,124</a>.</p>

        <p>That work shaped how he builds software: every number should trace back to a measurement, uncertainty should be stated out loud, and conclusions should change when the data does.</p>

        <p>The idea behind Lane Vector came from that background. Chemical kinetics describes how a reaction moves: its rate, its direction, and the forces that speed it up or slow it down. Lane Vector applies the same kind of math to how information and intent move between people and machines. TruVector puts it to work checking the information behind an AI&rsquo;s action before the action happens.</p>

        <p>InTellMe is self-funded and founder-run.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="room" id="properties" aria-labelledby="properties-title">
    <div class="suite suite--flagship">
      <p class="kicker">Active projects</p>
      <h2 class="suite-title reveal" id="properties-title">Everything we&rsquo;re working on.</h2>

      <ul class="properties reveal">
        <li class="property">
          <a class="property__link" href="https://www.lanevector.com" rel="noopener">lanevector.com</a>
          <span class="property__name">Lane Vector</span>
          <span class="property__note">The science of how information moves.</span>
        </li>
        <li class="property">
          <a class="property__link" href="https://truvector.science" rel="noopener">truvector.science</a>
          <span class="property__name">TruVector</span>
          <span class="property__note">A checkpoint an AI system runs before it acts.</span>
        </li>
        <li class="property">
          <a class="property__link" href="https://www.waether.space" rel="noopener">waether.space</a>
          <span class="property__name">wAether</span>
          <span class="property__note">Observatory of solar, galactic and terrestrial telemetry.</span>
        </li>
        <li class="property">
          <a class="property__link" href="https://savr.cam" rel="noopener">savr.cam</a>
          <span class="property__name">SAVR</span>
          <span class="property__note">Kitchen inventory and recipe planning.</span>
        </li>
        <li class="property">
          <a class="property__link" href="https://www.goldengoosetools.com" rel="noopener">goldengoosetools.com</a>
          <span class="property__name">Golden Goose Tools</span>
          <span class="property__note">Small tools for website owners, starting with a technical SEO audit.</span>
        </li>
        <li class="property">
          <a class="property__link" href="https://www.goldengoosetees.com" rel="noopener">goldengoosetees.com</a>
          <span class="property__name">Golden Goose Tees Studio</span>
          <span class="property__note">Design your own shirt with AI and order it printed and shipped.</span>
        </li>
        <li class="property">
          <a class="property__link" href="https://www.researchone.io/" rel="noopener">researchone.io</a>
          <span class="property__name">ResearchOne</span>
          <span class="property__note">A research workspace that keeps every source attached.</span>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="room" id="funding" aria-labelledby="funding-title">
    <div class="suite suite--flagship">
      <p class="kicker">Investors</p>
      <h2 class="suite-title reveal" id="funding-title">Self-funded so far. Raising a pre-seed round.</h2>
      <p class="reveal" style="margin-top:22px;max-width:62ch">InTellMe has been built without outside money. The round will pay for:</p>
      <ul class="reveal">
        <li>TruVector research and development</li>
        <li>Growing ResearchOne and SAVR</li>
        <li>Company operations</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="actions reveal" style="margin-top:24px">
        <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/investors#request">Request investor materials</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="room room--alt" id="contact" aria-labelledby="contact-title">
    <div class="suite suite--flagship">
      <p class="kicker">Contact</p>
      <h2 class="suite-title reveal" id="contact-title">Reach the person doing the work.</h2>

      <div class="contact reveal">
        <div class="contact__primary">
          <p class="contact__name">InTellMe</p>
          <address class="contact__address">
            326 Delaware Street<br />
            Johnson City, TN 37604<br />
            United States
          </address>
          <ul class="contact__lines">
            <li><span class="contact__label">Telephone</span><a href="tel:+17473221977">(747) 322-1977</a></li>
            <li><span class="contact__label">General</span><a href="mailto:info@intellmeai.com">info@intellmeai.com</a></li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="contact__directory">
          <div class="contact__col">
            <h3>Investors</h3>
            <ul>
              <li><a href="/investors#request">Request materials</a></li>
              <li><a href="mailto:info@intellmeai.com?subject=Investor%20materials">info@intellmeai.com</a></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="contact__col">
            <h3>Support</h3>
            <ul>
              <li><a href="mailto:support@intellmeai.com">support@intellmeai.com</a></li>
              <li><a href="mailto:billing@intellmeai.com">billing@intellmeai.com</a></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="contact__col">
            <h3>Security</h3>
            <ul>
              <li><a href="mailto:security@intellmeai.com">security@intellmeai.com</a></li>
              <li><a href="/.well-known/security.txt">security.txt</a></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="contact__col">
            <h3>Accessibility</h3>
            <ul>
              <li><a href="/accessibility">Accessibility statement</a></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</Base>

<style>
  .illustration-card__img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    margin: 0 0 18px;
    border: 1px solid var(--bronze-edge);
    border-radius: 2px;
  }
</style>
